ns or they're  gonna jack up the prices of their  ad-free plans even more and it's just a  matter of time until the streaming  services become indistinguishable from  regular television just with a modern  twist instead of having to watch on your  TV at a certain time you can watch on  any device at any time but that's pretty  much it one trick that still works is  the good old subscribe for a month and  cancel trick but streaming services are  well aware of this as well  this will probably just lead to more  shows being released at a pace of one  episode per week instead of the whole  season dropping it at the same time this  way they'll have a constant flow of  content the entire year and more people  will be enticed to stay subscribed and  at that point will truly be back to  Ground Zero as you would guess the vast  majority are not fans of the streaming  Evolution and the person they blame it  is Netflix obviously the situation is  not as simple as Netflix Being Greedy  but they've become an easy target so  when people see headlines that Netflix  is losing subscribers and that their  stock is performing worse than ever they  can't help but feel that Netflix got  what they deserved  foreign  despite all the doomsday headlines  Netflix simply isn't going anywhere so  far the entire subscriber loss is  equivalent to a measly 0.5 percent of  their total subscribers and that's with  every Factor working against them we've  got the Russian sanctions the post-covet  streaming Purge recession ludicrous  inflation and record high economic fears  if all of these factors are only leading  to Netflix losing 0.5 percent of their  subscribers this is clearly not that big  of a deal for Netflix long term this  isn't to say that Netflix is done losing  subscribers they have a quarterly report  coming out very soon and they may very  well report another loss and subscribers  for all I know they could post  subscriber losses for years to come but  eventually the economy will turn